<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Álmos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 820–c. 895</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Álmos, Grand Prince of the Hungarians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Álmos was a leader of the Hungarian tribal federation in the 9th century and the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arpad">Árpád</a>, founder of the Árpád dynasty. According to Hungarian tradition he was elected head of the seven tribes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etelkoz">Etelköz</a> and led them until shortly before the conquest of the Carpathian Basin around 895.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/almos.jpg" alt="Álmos" width="320" height="275" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Márk Kálti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%C3%A9pes_kr%C3%B3nika_-_21.oldal_-_%C3%81lmos_vez%C3%A9r.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
